    "freeTraits": 0,
    "biography": "<h2>Background</h2><p>Abraham DuSable is a distinguished Black Tremere whose family believed him murdered by the Ku Klux Klan shortly after World War I. In 1980, his mortal great-niece Carol Davis recognized him in a jazz club &mdash; he had not visibly aged in sixty years. Panicked and torn between fear of exposure and a desire he had never before felt, DuSable lost control of his Beast and nearly drained her, then fled after giving her a single drop of his vitae in a fit of guilt. The Brujah information broker Dickie, already watching DuSable on suspicion of Tremere manipulation in city politics, discovered the dying Davis and used the incident as leverage.</p><h2>Roleplaying Hints</h2><p>You carry guilt over Carol Davis like a stone around your neck. You are careful, controlled, and terrified of what happens if the Chantry &mdash; or Dickie &mdash; decides you are a liability.</p>",
    "notes": "A rare Tremere vulnerability: a living mortal relative (Carol Davis) who recognized him and now carries a drop of his vitae. The Brujah broker Dickie holds this secret as leverage.",
    "npcType": "vampire"
  },
